    "row": "| CFG937 | (block 930\u2013939; criteria 73144fddb; seal a8792e8b4, P937 sha256 75987b42\u2026; no amendments; agent lane, reviewed; not blind \u2014 formed after CFG934) two-floor primordial halos H-CF2: CFG934's cooling floor for dwarfs quenched at reionization + a filtering floor V_th = \u221a2 c_s(T_IGM) (CFG782's T_vir \u2265 T_IGM reused as a halo floor) for late formers; 36 corners: **(S) PARTIAL (corner-selectable) on both footings, FRAGILE** \u2014 LVD-83 +0.518 \u2192 \u22120.093\u2026+0.326 ln, CONSISTENT at 12/36 corners (CFG934: 0/12); classicals, M31 dSphs and SPARC untouched; all six classes consistent only at 3 settings (a discrete fit); the intermediate dSphs (\u221210 < M_V \u2264 \u22127.7) still keep +0.08\u2026+0.23 ln there, and where they come closest the ultra-faints are over-predicted (z \u22123.4); the L gain rests on giving the filtering floor to dwarfs whose SFH is only a group default (own-evidence selector \u2192 L CONTRADICTED 33/36). Coma UDGs, DF2/DF4 and tidal dwarfs: predicted 0 (unexplained). Sealed P937: at \u221210 < M_V \u2264 \u22127.7, late formers carry more excess than quenched dwarfs (+0.06\u2026+0.37 ln canonical; sign flips under reading M). K all pass; MUTATE_EQ pass; MUTATE_T10 FAILED as frozen (over-supply weakly detectable at some corners). **A second, filtering floor narrows CFG934's gap but does not close it robustly.** \u03ba = \u00bd FITTED; footings never pooled; not theory closed. | d1b1b476f |",
